# Content model

## Files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `copy.json` | UI chrome strings EN/PT (`nav`, `hero`, `work`, `catalog`, `timeline`, …) |
| `projects.json` | Featured **case studies** only (deep narrative) |
| `catalog.json` | Selected projects grid (archive) |
| `milestones.json` | Evolution timeline |
| `principles.json` | Principles list |

## Era ids (unified)

`design` | `hardware` | `ideyou` | `teaching` | `platform`

Do not use legacy aliases `craft` or `products` in new data.

## `projects.json` (case study)

```ts
{
  id: "cube" | "miodelivery" | "platform"
  accent: "yellow" | "green" | "coral" | …
  embed?: string
  title / subtitle / problem / difficulty / simplification / change: { en, pt }
  highlights?: { label: {en,pt}; value: {en,pt} }[]  // optional credibility strip
  chapters?: {
    title: {en,pt}
    body: {en,pt}
    steps?: {
      title: {en,pt}
      body: {en,pt}
      figure?: Figure  // nested beats under one numbered chapter
    }[]
    figure?: {
      type: "diagram" | "image" | "compare" | "carousel" | "photo" | "video"
      src?: string | { en: string; pt: string }
      poster?: string | { en: string; pt: string } // optional still for video
      fit?: "cover" // optional; default is width 100% + height auto (no crop)
      caption: {en,pt}
      items?: {
        src: string | {en,pt}
        type?: "video"
        poster?: string | {en,pt}
        label?: {en,pt}
        alt?: {en,pt}
      }[]  // compare (before/after) or carousel (multi-print / mixed media)
    }
  }[]
  links?: { live?: string; repo?: string; docs?: string }
  media?: { type: "image" | "video" | "diagram"; src: string | {en,pt}; alt?: { en, pt } }[]
}
```

Optional `highlights` / `chapters` (with optional `figure`) render in Featured (`#case-{id}`) and in the case modal. Keep the four classic beats as synthesis; chapters deepen the story. Prefer operational diagrams and screenshots as chapter figures — not brand-logo construction.

DOM anchor on Featured work: `#case-{id}` (page section). Catalog navigation uses `#project-{catalogId}` to open the modal.

## `catalog.json` (grid item)

```ts
{
  id: string
  era: EraId
  title: { en, pt }
  summary: { en, pt }
  detail?: { en, pt } // longer body inside the project modal
  language: string
  tech?: string[]
  links?: { live?: string; repo?: string; docs?: string } // docs = extra file/PDF opened from the modal
  caseId?: "cube" | "miodelivery" | "platform"
  accent: "yellow" | "green" | "coral" | "red" | "blue" | "orange"
  logo?: string // project logo/favicon URL; falls back to monogram if missing or broken
  logoBg?: string // CSS color behind the logo (for light/white logos), e.g. "#0a0a0a"
  pinnedEnd?: boolean // always rendered last in the grid, regardless of array edits / filters
  linkLabels?: { live?: {en,pt}; repo?: {en,pt} } // override Live/Repo link text
  media?: { type: "image" | "video"; src: string; alt?: { en, pt } }[]
}
```

Visual identity: era color (CSS) + accent + real project logo (favicon) when available, monogram from title as fallback — not a shared generic CDN icon for every card.

Opening a catalog card sets `#project-{id}` and opens the detail modal. Items with `caseId` get the larger case modal (carousel + narrative from `projects.json`). Card footer Live/Repo remain direct external links.

## `milestones.json`

```ts
{
  id: EraId          // same as era
  era: EraId
  years: string
  title: { en, pt }  // short poetic
  headline: { en, pt } // factual subtitle
  body: { en, pt }     // short lead
  context: { en, pt }  // longer visitor context
  projects: string[]   // catalog ids
}
```

## Copy keys for catalog / timeline

- `catalog.eyebrow`, `catalog.title`, `catalog.lead`
- `catalog.filters.all` + `catalog.filters.{era}`
- `catalog.caseStudy`, `catalog.viewCase`, `catalog.live`, `catalog.repo`
- `timeline.lead` may mention thinking milestones with real context

Always author both `en` and `pt`. No machine-translation pipeline.
